{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3426","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3426","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3426\",\"parent_revision\":\"1936d2cfcb63ac7fedc978a422eb66a44a5e9268069141fcbdd031a31c87a6bf\",\"root_revision\":\"1936d2cfcb63ac7fedc978a422eb66a44a5e9268069141fcbdd031a31c87a6bf\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ndevelopment-harness is distributed. Its runtime text is read by an agent whose working directory is the consuming repo, which never had this repo checked out. `rules/runtime-vs-design-time.md` requires every path in runtime text to be universally present, inside the artifact's own bundled files, or inlined. 37 do not meet that bar.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: an installed consumer following one of these instructions reaches a path that does not exist. It resolves in the authoring checkout and nowhere else, so the failure appears only for real users of the plugin and never for anyone testing from this repo.\\n\\nScanner: `scripts/audit_dh_runtime_escapes.py`, stdlib-only, exit 0 when clean. Regenerate with:\\n`uv run python3 scripts/audit_dh_runtime_escapes.py --out .tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-dh-runtime-escapes.md`\\n\\nFull report with file:line detail for every finding: `.tmp/scratch/reports/20260906-dh-runtime-escapes.md`\\n\\nTOTALS (2026-09-06) \u2014 37 escapes across 18 files:\\n- `repo-path` 23 \u2014 paths into the authoring tree (`scripts/\u2026`, `rules/\u2026`, `docs/\u2026`)\\n- `cross-plugin-skill` 10 \u2014 `<plugin>:<skill>` activations of another plugin; 9 carry no guard word on the line\\n- `cross-plugin-path` 4 \u2014 filesystem paths into a sibling plugin\\n- `design-time-link` 0\\n\\nWorst files: `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/default-development-flow.md` (5), `skills/evaluate-sdlc-layers/SKILL.md` (4), `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md` (4).\\n\\nConfirmed real cross-plugin skill references include `agent-orchestration:agent-orchestration` (2, in skills/dispatch \u2014 already tracked for reroute), `python3-development:stinkysnake`, `agentskill-kaizen:transcript-analyst`, and `plugin-creator:hook-creator` (guarded).\\n\\nScanner precision, stated honestly: cross-plugin skill detection uses an allowlist derived from the actual `plugins/` directory listing, so label values (`state:verified`) and template placeholders (`plugin:skill-name`) are excluded. Fenced code blocks are skipped. Two known false-positive classes remain and should be triaged rather than fixed blindly: illustrative paths inside markdown table cells (e.g. `plugins/dh/scripts/migrate.py` in a regex-pattern table in code-review-architecture), and deliberately generic examples such as `scripts/foo.py`. Guard detection for cross-plugin references is a same-line keyword scan; it triages, it does not decide.\\n\\nExit criterion: the scanner reports 0 and is promoted to a drift test beside `tests/test_status_label_registry_drift.py`. Fixing per the rule means inlining the content, moving it into the artifact's own `references/`, or making a cross-plugin reference conditional on that plugin being installed.\\n\\nUser-provided context: nothing was fixed in this pass by instruction. The script is the durable artifact.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: scripts/audit_dh_runtime_escapes.py, session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a63b0f10cf9eeb716b60ecb32da499ebbed75114221ecf5007500275d778eb89\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTNew\"}"}